# Copy to .env (git ignores it) and fill in what you need; npm start reads it.

# bergfex currently serves tour GPX files without a login, about 40 per 20 minutes. If it starts asking for a login,
# or to see whether your account gets more, log in on bergfex.at in your browser, open the developer tools' Network
# tab, reload a bergfex page, and copy the value of the request's "Cookie" header here. It is only sent with the
# GPX downloads, and you can delete it any time.
# BERGFEX_COOKIE=

# PORT=5173

# key for uploading the Sentinel-2 mosaics to the public site (node --env-file=.env scripts/s2-mosaic.js upload ...),
# e.g. from openssl rand -hex 32; its SHA-256 goes into wrangler.toml as UPLOAD_KEY_SHA256
# UPLOAD_KEY=
